    "sections": [
      {
        "body": "Three descriptive questions use ES, NQ and GC two-minute bars: whether persistent versus rotational VWAP states retain the next thirty-minute residence; whether opposing price/VWAP slopes predict crossing; and whether frozen VWAP or TWAP better locates the median of future thirty-minute one-minute closes. The atlas pools products only as specified in the saved run; errors below keep products separate.",
        "id": "question",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Question and scope"
      },
      {
        "body": "The raw state and slope gaps shrink after matching shared context. The pooled primary fair-price comparison favors VWAP, but Asia and New York local-anchor checks favor TWAP. Last-known price has smaller absolute error than either reference. Barrier follow-ups do not establish a trading rule.",
        "id": "findings",
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Supported findings"
      },
